## Phase 9: Preserve overlapping tiles during map view changes

Depends on Phases 5–8.

Outcome: panning and zooming retain valid presentation and GPU inputs for tiles that remain visible, without disappearing and reappearing solely because the visible set changed.

- [ ] Replace whole-view receipt clearing and pending-request dropping with incremental entering/retained/leaving tile handling. Retain valid receipts and useful in-flight work for overlapping tiles; request newly visible or genuinely invalidated inputs. Update screen placement and zoom independently of environmental input validity.
- [ ] Separate world/purge/source validity from view membership. Cancel or deprioritize work that left the view without revoking still-needed work; admit late completions only when their source provenance is current and the tile is applicable to the current view. Preserve current explored-coverage checks immediately before drawing.
- [ ] Protect retained visible regional/tile snapshots, bundles and GPU resources during view transitions. Remove or evict off-view entries before unchanged overlapping entries as needed; prevent admission order or cache shrink from causing eviction/reload cascades. Keep retention and queue admission bounded under explicit policies; do not add speculative prefetch or remote retrieval.
- [ ] Reuse unchanged regional, elevation, coverage and ocean-classification textures across scrolling and zooming. Re-read or upload only newly needed, changed or legitimately evicted inputs. Preserve targeted regional/tile invalidation, normal per-frame GPU comparison and rendering, and shared-pass state ownership.
- [ ] Retain close/reopen, tab/minimap eligibility, shader reload, purge, world-switch and shutdown behavior. Stopping disposable presentation must still preserve pending environmental writes and reject stale world/purge results.
- [ ] Add focused regressions for partially overlapping pans in both directions, rapid leave/re-entry, zoom/view shrink, unchanged tile sets with changed screen positions, and views larger than cache floors. Verify unchanged overlapping tiles keep their receipts/source identities, remain drawable without reacquisition gaps, and incur no unnecessary local reads or texture uploads. Cover queued completions, source/ocean updates and stale coverage independently.
- [ ] Use subagents for focused tests and canonical build/package checks. Verify stable scrolling through the normal map/RenderDoc workflow without permanent diagnostic readbacks or a standalone graphics harness. Reconcile [HabitatEvaluation.md](HabitatEvaluation.md), proposal performance/lifecycle requirements and Integration contracts 7–8. Leave representative resource/frame-time measurement to Phase 10.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Source review, focused reuse/invalidation evidence and normal-map verification show that overlapping valid tiles remain available during view changes; newly visible tiles acquire normally, obsolete results cannot leak into current coverage, and bounded cache transitions avoid unnecessary rereads/reuploads. Linked documentation and build/package receipts are current; measured performance claims remain separate.

Implementation traceability: tasks 1–4 map to [HabitatEvaluation.md](HabitatEvaluation.md#incremental-view-retention), the proposal's performance/lifecycle expectations and Integration contract 8. Presentation now changes membership incrementally without cancelling overlapping receipts or dropping useful pending tasks. Preparation checks membership separately from its presentation lifetime and storage/source provenance, and skips departed jobs before reads, between reads and before publication. Regional/tile/bundle/receipt/texture caches install visible-key protection before shrink/admission, selecting off-view victims regardless of recency. Texture keys retain coordinate and exact source lease identity; screen placement/zoom remain frame inputs. New regressions check the first changed-view frame, both pan directions, shrink above cache floors, placement-only changes, coverage removal/re-entry, ocean-only invalidation, blocked queued work and the real graphics owner's cache-hit path without a GL context.

Task 5 maps to Integration contracts 7–8, [EnvironmentalStorage.md](EnvironmentalStorage.md#ordering-and-lifetime) and the proposal's persistence/lifecycle requirements. Explicit close still revokes the presentation lifetime, clears graphics/receipts and returns source retention to floors without stopping durable acquisition. Reopen can reuse current original sources; shader reload leaves them intact. Purge/source commits/world shutdown retain their separate lease/epoch checks. Existing persistence, full-map applicability, shared-pass and lifecycle regressions remain applicable.

Tasks 6–7 and completion inherit the user-run stable-scrolling gate as well as focused/full-suite/build/package checks. Second source review and an independent completion audit find no confirmed implementation defect or linked-document traceability gap. The audit independently consulted the phase hierarchy, full proposal, HabitatEvaluation, Integration contracts 7–8, storage/acquisition lifecycle documentation and applicable API source. Final subagent validation passes 96 focused EcosystemMap tests and 2,162 full-suite tests. Commands: `dotnet test VanillaExpanded.Tests/VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj --no-restore -p:UseSharedCompilation=false --filter FullyQualifiedName~EcosystemMap`, the same without the filter, and canonical `./build.ps1 --configuration=Release`, with `VINTAGE_STORY=G:/Vintagestory`, `NUGET_PACKAGES=C:/Users/Sisco/.nuget/packages` and game Lib on PATH. JSON validation/build/package pass; existing unrelated C# and Cake Pkcs warnings remain. ZIP `Releases/vanillaexpanded_999.99.9.zip`: 1,980,225 bytes, SHA-256 `A95603A2170B5C32EEA688E22FFD4C1EC42738470B56869869CAEDB1C36D8137`. Packaged DLL matches Release output (SHA-256 `4243BA408ABD5655C960A956871795ECAD5E3C0013CD85F559C85FC8BEAF3FC7`); both habitat shaders match source.

Remaining evidence gap: normal user-run stable scrolling through the full-map Ecosystem overlay after **Install development mod**. The requested check covers both pan directions, zoom in/out, continuously retained overlapping overlays and normal acquisition of entering tiles. All Phase 9 markers remain unchecked until this required case is confirmed and the audit rechecks it. No fresh capture, standalone harness or permanent diagnostic readback is required or claimed. No representative resource or frame-time improvement is claimed; those measurements remain in Phase 10.

## Phase 10: Validate the integrated feature and reconcile documentation

Depends on Phases 1–9.

Outcome: completion is supported by separate automated, packaged, performance, and live visual evidence.

- [ ] Use subagents for required build/test tools, following repository instructions. Record exact commands, target version, results, and limitations; resolve failures before marking related work complete.
- [ ] Verify client/server packaging and registration using the repository's existing workflow, including shrub-delivery support and operation of unrelated features when that support is absent.
- [ ] Exercise the integrated lifecycle across redraw, map close/reopen, unload, reconnect, purge, version changes, normal shutdown with pending writes, and server/world switches. Confirm ecosystem storage never accesses vanilla's database.
- [ ] Measure map opening, panning, species switching, environmental capture, shrub delivery, CPU cache size and GPU resource usage on representative explored maps. Include view/selection costs and texture reuse; record workloads and measured results, and adjust bounds based on evidence before claiming suitable limits or frame-time performance.
- [ ] Obtain user-run in-game acceptance for readable terrain, dropdown visibility and selection retention, stable habitat highlighting, and red crosshatching in mixed-coverage views. Do not launch the game on the user's behalf for visual acceptance.
- [ ] Confirm live disappearance of crosshatching as inputs arrive; confirm no overlay on unexplored terrain, minimap, or inactive tab, including after full-map close. Confirm old uncached areas remain unavailable until normally revisited.
- [ ] Update permanent feature documentation to describe implemented behavior, missing-data presentation, server support, dedicated cache, and no-backfill limits. Keep historical/staging details in planning evidence only.
- [ ] Reconcile the implementation and completion receipts against every proposal requirement and this checklist. Keep unmet gates unchecked; report blockers rather than replacing required runtime evidence with headless checks.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Build/test and package receipts, measured performance evidence, and user-run visual acceptance are separately recorded and satisfactory; no required gate remains pending.

## Final acceptance

- [ ] Every proposal requirement is mapped to completed work above; only the explicitly deferred supplemental server catalogue remains outside scope.
- [ ] Persistent environmental data survives normal lifecycle transitions; disposable work can be discarded; explicit purge clears feature-owned state.
- [ ] Full-map-only suitable/unavailable presentation, species scope, original shrub delivery, separate storage, and no-backfill behavior meet the proposal.
- [ ] Linked documentation and checklist reflect verified completion without overstating source inspection, automated checks, or live-runtime evidence.
